ink>(accessed April 2008).</citation></ref><ref id="b14-ijerph-06-00694"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Goldberg</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><name><surname>Burnett</surname><given-names>RT</given-names></name><name><surname>Bailar</surname><given-names>JC</given-names><suffix>III</suffix></name><name><surname>Tamblyn</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Ernst</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Flegel</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Brook</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Bonvalot</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Singh</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Valois</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name><name><surname>Vincent</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Identification of persons with cardiorespiratory conditions who are at risk of dying from the acute effects of ambient air particles</article-title><source>Environ. Health Perspect</source><year>2001</year><volume>109</volume><fpage>487</fpage><lpage>494</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11544152</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b15-ijerph-06-00694"><label>15.</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gosselin</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>B&#x000e9;langer</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Doyon</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Health Impacts of climate change in Quebec, Chap. 6</article-title><source>Human Health in a Changing Climate: A Canadian Assessment of Vulnerabilities and Adaptive Capacity</source><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>S&#x000e9;guin</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><publisher-name>Health Canada</publisher-name><publisher-loc>Ottawa, Canada</publisher-loc><year>2008</year><fpage>211</fpage><lpage>302</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b16-ijerph-06-00694"><label>16.</label><citation citation-type="web"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>B&#x000e9;langer</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Gosselin</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Valois</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Abdous</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><source>Vagues de froid au Qu&#x000e9;bec m&#x000e9;ridional: adaptations actuelles et suggestions d'adaptations futures</source><year>2006</year><fpage>183</fpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.inspq.qc.ca/pdf/publications/537-VaguesFroid_Quebec.pdf">http://www.inspq.qc.ca/pdf/publications/537-VaguesFroid_Quebec.pdf</ext-link> (accessed April 2008).</citation></ref><ref id="b17-ijerph-06-00694"><label>17.</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Alavi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Beaumont</surname><given-names>J-F</given-names></name></person-group><source>Evaluation and adjustment for non-response in the Canadian Labour Force Survey</source><publisher-name>Statistics Canada</publisher-name><publisher-loc>Ottawa, Canada</publisher-loc><year>2003</year><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.statcan.ca/bsolc/english/bsolc?catno=11-522-X20030017598">http://www.statcan.ca/bsolc/english/bsolc?catno=11-522-X20030017598</ext-link> (accessed April 2008).</citation></ref><ref id="b18-ijerph-06-00694"><label>18.</label><citation citation-type="web"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Institut de la statistique du Qu&#x000e9;bec</collab></person-group><source>Recensement de la population 2001 : le Qu&#x000e9;bec</source><year>2001</year><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.stat.gouv.qc.ca/regions/lequebec/quebec_index.htm#population">http://www.stat.gouv.qc.ca/regions/lequebec/quebec_index.htm#population</ext-link> (accessed April 2008).</citation></ref><ref id="b19-ijerph-06-00694"><label>19.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thompson</surname><given-names>SK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Sample size for estimating multinomial proportions</article-title><source>Amer. Statist</source><year>1987</year><volume>41</volume><fpage>42</fpage><lpage>46</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b20-ijerph-06-00694"><label>20.</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Presser</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Rothqeb</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Couper</surname><given-names>MP</given-names></name><name><surname>Lessler</surname><given-names>JT</given-names></name><name><surname>Martin</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Singer</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><source>Methods for testing and evaluating survey questionnaires</source><publisher-name>John Wiley &#x00026; Sons</publisher-name><publisher-loc>Chichester, UK</publisher-loc><year>2004</year><fpage>624</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="b21-ijerph-06-00694"><label>21.</label><citation citation-type="web"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Statistics Canada</collab></person-group><source>Households and the Environment 2006</source>Statistics Canada, Canada,<year>2007</year><fpage>65</fpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.statcan.ca/english/freepub/11-526-XIE/11-526-XIE2007001.pdf">http://www.statcan.ca/english/freepub/11-526-XIE/11-526-XIE2007001.pdf</ext-link> (accessed April 2008).</citation></ref><ref id="b22-ijerph-06-00694"><label>22.</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Scherrer</surname><given-names>B</given-names></n